{
  "enabled": true,
  "name": "Code Quality Analyzer",
  "description": "Monitors source code files for changes and analyzes them for potential improvements including code smells, design patterns, best practices, readability, maintainability, and performance optimizations",
  "version": "1",
  "when": {
    "type": "fileCreated",
    "patterns": []
  },
  "then": {
    "type": "askAgent",
    "prompt": "Analyze the modified code files for potential improvements. Focus on:\n\n1. **Code Smells**: Identify any code smells such as:\n   - Long functions/methods that should be broken down\n   - Duplicate code that could be extracted\n   - Complex conditionals that could be simplified\n   - Magic numbers/strings that should be constants\n   - Overly nested code structures\n\n2. **Design Patterns**: Suggest appropriate design patterns where applicable:\n   - Factory, Strategy, Observer, Decorator patterns\n   - Dependency injection opportunities\n   - Separation of concerns improvements\n\n3. **Best Practices**: Check adherence to:\n   - Python: PEP 8, type hints, docstrings, error handling\n   - TypeScript/React: Component composition, hooks usage, prop types, error boundaries\n   - FastAPI: Proper dependency injection, schema validation, async/await patterns\n   - Next.js: Server/client component usage, data fetching patterns, route organization\n\n4. **Readability**: Evaluate:\n   - Variable and function naming clarity\n   - Code organization and structure\n   - Comment quality and necessity\n   - Function/method length and complexity\n\n5. **Maintainability**: Assess:\n   - Code modularity and reusability\n   - Coupling and cohesion\n   - Test coverage opportunities\n   - Documentation completeness\n\n6. **Performance**: Identify optimization opportunities:\n   - Database query optimization (N+1 queries, missing indexes)\n   - Unnecessary re-renders in React components\n   - Inefficient algorithms or data structures\n   - Caching opportunities\n   - Async/await usage in Python\n\nProvide specific, actionable suggestions with code examples where helpful. Maintain the existing functionality while improving code quality. Prioritize changes by impact (high/medium/low)."
  }
}